+## The window
+
+The tt window is a local HTML page beside the session: it shows what you send
+it, asks your questions with buttons, lets the engineer read status,
+connections and docs, and takes typed questions. It is optional; without it,
+everything here works in the terminal as written.
+
+For `window`, run:
+
+```sh
+bash "<skill folder>/scripts/guide.sh" window open
+```
+
+It opens the page in the browser and shows the greeting and where the documents
+in this folder stand. Exit 3 means no Python: say the window isn't available
+here, and carry on in the terminal. Then say in one line that questions will be
+asked in the window, and that `/tt-guide window` reopens it.
+
+At the start of any other flow, check once:
+`bash "<skill folder>/scripts/guide.sh" window status`. Exit 1 (`not open`) means
+no window: ignore the rest of this section. While it is open:
+
+- **Questions.** Ask each yes/no or choice question (the update go-ahead, the
+  connections playback, replacing a pack, init's "go through the gaps?") through
+  the window, with the questions as JSON on stdin in the AskUserQuestion shape:
+
+  ```sh
+  bash "<skill folder>/scripts/guide.sh" window ask <<'Q'
+  {"questions":[{"question":"Happy for me to go ahead?","header":"Update","multiSelect":false,
+    "options":[{"label":"Go ahead","description":"pull and fix the links"},{"label":"No","description":"change nothing"}]}]}
+  Q
+  ```
+
+  It prints `<header><TAB><answer>` per question. Only the "yes" option itself
+  is an explicit yes; anything typed under Other is the engineer's own words, to
+  read as you would in chat. Exit 5: say in one line that you are waiting in the
+  window, then run `window answer <id>` with the printed id; after three of
+  those, ask in chat instead. Exit 6 (declined) or any other failure: ask in chat.
+- **Showing.** Put what's worth reading in the window as well as in chat: the
+  connections playback, `about` and `start` output, a longer answer. Pipe it in:
+  `... | bash "<skill folder>/scripts/guide.sh" window show markdown "<title>"`
+  (`text` for plain output). Keep the chat reply to a line and the command to
+  type.
+- **Typed questions.** If `window status` said `attached (claude mod)`, the
+  window's messages reach you as ordinary prompts: do nothing extra. Otherwise,
+  after each answer run `bash "<skill folder>/scripts/guide.sh" window listen`
+  and answer what it prints as if it were typed here. Exit 5 (nothing yet):
+  listen again, at most five times in a row, then say "The window's quiet; type
+  here, or ask me to listen again." and stop.
+- Never send a token, password or key to the window, and never ask for one there.
+
 ## Greet
 
 Show the greeting to the user exactly as it is, the robot in a code block,
